# Canonical study dragonfly for the ss-dragonfly fixtures and sanity
# harnesses: p = 2 hosts per router, a = 2 routers per group, h = 1
# global link per router, g = a*h + 1 = 3 groups; 6 routers, 12 hosts.
# All link classes run at 200 Gbit/s; the Rosetta-class switch pipeline
# uses the 350 ns mean latency reported for the physical Rosetta ASIC
# (De Sensi et al., SC'20, section II-A).
#
# Status: hosted, calibration pending.  Congestion quantizers and the
# advertisement cadence are named calibrated abstractions; see
# docs/ss-dragonfly-fabric/README.md.
topology dragonfly
hosts_per_router 2
routers_per_group 2
global_links_per_router 1
groups 3
host_link_gbps 200
local_link_gbps 200
global_link_gbps 200
host_link_latency_ps 300000
local_link_latency_ps 300000
global_link_latency_ps 1000000
switch_pipeline_ps 350000
rosetta_buffer_bytes 4194304
max_wire_packet_bytes 4160
near_end_bytes_per_level 8320
far_end_bytes_per_level 8320
downstream_bytes_per_level 33280
advertisement_period_ps 10000000
advertisement_delay_ps 1000000
maximum_downstream_age_ps 40000000
routing_seed 383530136519245852
